; ⚠️ THE WESTERN SEAM WAS UNDER WATER AND NOW IS NOT (Phase 44). The tarn used to be a 20 m band down
; the whole west edge of the cell, so the seam with wilds_west — which meets this cell at local
; (-26, 0) — was open lake. The bay is now an L that leaves a shore road along the north, and the two
; road segments below run from the town seam at local z = -8 to the wilds seam at local z = 0.
;
; The hamlet is NOT on that road: it sits on a spit the bay wraps on three sides, reached by a 6 m
