; ====================================================================================================
; THE MAP (38F, 2026-08-09). Re-laid at the maintainer's direction after a play-through: the settled
; cells now form ONE CONTIGUOUS CITY in the middle and every wilds cell sits outside it.
;
;                                     arena          (0, -160)   z -178..-142
;                                wilds_north         (0, -117)   z -142..-92
;                              crossway_post         (0,  -66)   z  -92..-40
;   wilds_west     tarn_landing        TOWN_HUB          emberdeep_mine
;   (-107, -6)      (-56, -6)          (0, -10)            (56, -10)
;                  hollowreach        embermarket
;                   (-52, 46)          (0, 46)
;
; ⚠️ EVERY CENTRE HERE IS ARITHMETIC, NOT TASTE. A cell floor is centred on its own origin, so two
; cells abut when |dz| = (depth_a + depth_b) / 2. A gap is a hole the player falls through; an overlap
; is two coplanar floors z-fighting along the seam; and NEITHER IS VISIBLE FROM THIS FILE. Floors, all
; measured in-engine: town_hub 60x60, arena 36x36, wilds_north 50x50, wilds_west 50x40, everything
; else 52x52. Every seam below is a full shared edge, not a corner touch:
;
;   town_hub   x -30..30, z -40..20     the anchor - it does NOT move, because SpawnPoint,
;                                       SafeZoneCenter and the cottage property all read off it
;   embermarket        z  20..72        abuts the hub's south edge          (unchanged)
;   hollowreach  x -78..-26, z 20..72   abuts the market's west edge at x = -26, and shares 48 m of
;                                       its north edge with Tarn's Landing
;   tarn_landing x -82..-30, z -32..20  abuts the hub's west edge at x = -30
;   wilds_west  x -132..-82             abuts Tarn's west edge at x = -82
;   emberdeep_mine x 30..82             abuts the hub's east edge at x = 30
;   crossway_post      z -92..-40       abuts the hub's north edge at z = -40
;   wilds_north        z -142..-92      abuts the gate
;   arena              z -178..-142     abuts the northern wilds, 150 m from the town square
;
; WHAT CHANGED AND WHY, because two of these reverse decisions this file used to argue for:
;
; 1. ⚠️ THE ARENA WAS AT (55, -10) - SIXTY-FIVE METRES FROM THE TOWN SQUARE, sitting on the road
;    between the town and the mine. A boss arena is not a suburb. It is now the far end of the
;    northern road, past the gate and past the wilds, and it is the last cell in the realm.
;
; 2. ⚠️ HOLLOWREACH WAS AT (-106, 74), separated from everything by 32 m of nothing. This file used
;    to argue that gap was deliberate - "two settlements on one shore should not share a property
;    line". Played, it just read as a cell that had fallen off the map. It is now the city's dockside
;    district, abutting the market.
;
; 3. ⚠️ THE WILDS USED TO SIT BETWEEN SETTLEMENTS, and this file used to argue that too: the road
;    from the town to the gate ran through wilds_north, which is what made the Crossway toll read as
;    something the wardens were owed. THAT ARGUMENT IS NOW GONE - the gate abuts the town directly.
;    The toll still stands on what is BEYOND the gate rather than before it: the wilds and the arena
;    are on the far side, so the wardens hold the last safe ground before the frontier. If the toll
;    ever stops reading, this is the paragraph that explains why.
;
; Hollowreach keeps SafeRadius 0. It is a city district now, but a smugglers' wharf the wardens do
; not visit still has no business being safe ground, and the region's own 34 m bubble is centred on
; the square 74 m away, so nothing covers it.
;
; ⚠️ SURPLUS AND DEMAND (38G), AND THE EMPTY LISTS ARE AS DELIBERATE AS THE FULL ONES. Only two cells
; author anything: the mine is awash in ore, metal and fuel and short of everything that has to be
; carried up to it; the Landing is the mirror, awash in fish and short of everything the mine digs up.
; The town square and the Embermarket author NOTHING, because they are the reference the other two are
; read against - a multiplier applied everywhere is a multiplier nowhere, which is the sentence 38G
; was parked on for eleven sub-phases. Hollowreach authors nothing either, for a different reason:
; HollowreachHull.tres explains why its economics are deliberately flat at every tier, and a fence
; whose prices moved with the local trade would be a fence with an opinion about the local trade.
;
; ⚠️ SHOCK CANDIDATES (38T), AND THEY ARE THE THIRD LIST RATHER THAN A SETTING ON THE FIRST TWO. A
; shock moves a tag OUT of one of the lists above and INTO the other for two to five days, so a
; candidate is only an event where it inverts what the cell already says: the mine can be cut off from
; the ore under its own feet (the seam floods) or finally see a food cart get through, and the Landing
; is the mirror - the boats stay in, or a train of ore carts arrives. A candidate the cell already
; treats the shocked way is a notice on the board announcing that nothing has happened, which is what
; SupplyShockRules.Roll and --validate both refuse.
;
; ONLY THE TWO CELLS THAT AUTHOR TRADE AUTHOR SHOCKS, and that is the same argument as above rather
; than a smaller version of it: a shock at the Embermarket would move prices at thirteen shops that
; all price at par by CellId, so it would move nothing until every one of them was pointed at the cell
; - and 38G's trap is precisely that a half-authored settlement is invisible. A fair belongs at a
; market and this is where it will go when those shops are placed; here, a "fair" is a caravan
; arriving at a mine that had run short, which is the same event wearing work clothes.
;
; The two lists are a PAIR and have to be read together: a carry only pays when the source has the
; surplus and the destination the demand, because the buy/sell spread it has to clear is about 1.84x
; at a specialist. See RegionDemand for the arithmetic and the factors.
; ====================================================================================================

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Cell_town_hub"]
script = ExtResource("2_cell")
Id = "ember_crown.town_hub"
ScenePath = "res://scenes/regions/ember_crown/town_hub.tscn"
Center = Vector3(0, 0, -10)
Presentation = SubResource("Presentation_town_hub")

; The Embermarket (Phase 38K). Placed so its 52 m square ABUTS the town hub's 60 m one exactly: the hub
; floor runs to z = 20, and a 52-wide floor centred at z = 46 starts there. A gap is a hole the player
; falls through; an overlap is two coplanar floors z-fighting along a seam. Neither is visible in the
; editor from a .tres, so the arithmetic is written down here rather than eyeballed.
;
; 38M2 removed every LoadRadius here: the streamer no longer decides anything by distance, so all eight
; cells are resident from the moment the region is entered.
;
; SafeRadius 32 is the field 38K added: a settlement can be more than one cell, and the region's own
; 34 m bubble around the square cannot reach a district a street away without also swallowing the wilds
; cells the encounters live in. The two bubbles overlap between z = 14 and z = 24, so there is no strip
; of unprotected ground between the square and the market for a warband to spawn into.

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Cell_embermarket"]
script = ExtResource("2_cell")
Id = "ember_crown.embermarket"
ScenePath = "res://scenes/regions/ember_crown/embermarket.tscn"
Center = Vector3(0, 0, 46)
Presentation = SubResource("Presentation_embermarket")
SafeRadius = 32.0

; The Crossway Post (Phase 38M2). Placed so its 52 m square ABUTS wilds_north's 50 m one exactly:
; wilds_north is centred at z = -65 and its floor ends at z = -90, and a 52-wide floor centred at
; z = -116 starts there. Same arithmetic 38K did for the Embermarket, and for the same reason — a gap
; is a hole the player falls through and an overlap is two coplanar floors z-fighting along the seam,
; and neither is visible from this file.
;
[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Cell_crossway_post"]
script = ExtResource("2_cell")
Id = "ember_crown.crossway_post"
ScenePath = "res://scenes/regions/ember_crown/crossway_post.tscn"
Center = Vector3(0, 0, -66)
Presentation = SubResource("Presentation_crossway")
SafeRadius = 26.0

; The Emberdeep Mine (Phase 38N1). Placed so its 52 m square ABUTS the arena's 36 m one exactly: the
; arena is centred at x = 55 and its floor ends at x = 73, and a 52-wide floor centred at x = 99 starts
; there. Same arithmetic as the Embermarket and the Crossway Post, for the same reason.
;
[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Cell_emberdeep_mine"]
script = ExtResource("2_cell")
Id = "ember_crown.emberdeep_mine"
ScenePath = "res://scenes/regions/ember_crown/emberdeep_mine.tscn"
Center = Vector3(56, 0, -10)
Presentation = SubResource("Presentation_mine")
SafeRadius = 24.0
Surplus = Array[String](["ore", "metal", "fuel"])
Demand = Array[String](["food", "fish", "textile"])
ShockTags = Array[String](["ore", "food"])

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Cell_wilds_north"]
script = ExtResource("2_cell")
Id = "ember_crown.wilds_north"
ScenePath = "res://scenes/regions/ember_crown/wilds_north.tscn"
Center = Vector3(0, 0, -117)
Presentation = SubResource("Presentation_wilds_north")

; Tarn's Landing (Phase 38N2). Placed so its 52 m square ABUTS wilds_west's 50 m one exactly:
; wilds_west is centred at x = -55 and its floor ends at x = -80, and a 52-wide floor centred at
; x = -106 starts there. Third time this arithmetic has been written down and third time it has been
; right, which is the argument for writing it down.
;
[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Cell_tarn_landing"]
script = ExtResource("2_cell")
Id = "ember_crown.tarn_landing"
ScenePath = "res://scenes/regions/ember_crown/tarn_landing.tscn"
Center = Vector3(-56, 0, -6)
Presentation = SubResource("Presentation_tarn")
SafeRadius = 22.0
